      },
      "message": "feat(post): write an inverted machine axis mirrored - sign, I/J/K, G2/G3, G41/G42\n\nThe engine mirrors the record stream once (post::invert) for a machine\nwhose X and/or Y is inverted. Coordinates, arc centres, the Start chain\nand the work-offset origin on that axis negate, and the stock box edges\nswap. An arc in a plane holding exactly one inverted axis reverses (G2 <->\nG3). XY cutter compensation swaps sides (G41 <-> G42) when exactly one of\nX and Y is inverted. A standard machine's records are untouched.\n\nRefused by name, nothing posted: an inverted Z or any other letter, a\nscript without axisInversion = true (only Fanuc and Haas declare it),\nhelical arcs, threading cycles, tilted A/B/C moves, C-axis live tooling,\nprobing, an unpaired stock edge, and a static axis stating reversal.\n\nPinned by inverted-X Fanuc/Haas goldens and by a controller-\ninterpretation equivalence test (inverted X, Y and X+Y): the posted\nprogram read by the inverted controller follows the CAM path within\n0.002 mm, and the untranslated program does not.\n\nFixes #374\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
